# Behaviour fixture for the cloudflare spend-belt alerts (#217) — FU-158's behaviour half, and the
# #288/#313/#328 restart-gap class ported to this directory in homelab#334.
#
#   devbox run -- promtool test rules argocd/resources/cloudflare-exporter/spend-belt.promtool-test
#
# The FIRST fixture in this directory. Named .promtool-test, not .yaml: manifest-lint kubeconforms
# every *.yaml under argocd/resources. CI-enforced since 2026-08-11: .github/workflows/ci.yaml runs
# `devbox run prometheus-rules-lint`, which runs `promtool test rules` over every *.promtool-test
# under argocd/.
# CLOCK: promtool's test clock starts at 0. Range selectors are LEFT-OPEN in Prometheus 3.x, so
# `[10m]` at t sees (t-10m, t] — a last real sample at T stays in range through T+9m at a 1m
# interval and is gone at T+10m. Every boundary claim below is pinned by a promql_expr_test rather
# than counted in a comment.
#
# ✅ WHAT THIS FILE RESOLVES (homelab#334): all three spend-belt alerts sit on gauges scraped from
# `replicas: 1` Deployments (cloudflare-exporter and cloudflare-spend-probe — both confirmed
# `kube_deployment_spec_replicas == 1` live on 2026-08-12), so every one of them carried BOTH
# halves of the #288 defect: `pod`/`instance` on the series gave the alert a churning identity, and
# a single replica means the vector empties outright while the new pod starts. A roll therefore
# restarted a `for:` window measuring a condition that never stopped being true — a billing toggle
# and a plan change persist until a human reverts them, and a blind probe stays blind.
# Fixed with the #288 two-part shape, `max|min by (zone)` + `max|min_over_time([10m])`.
#
# THREE things here are NOT a mechanical port of #328, and each is a test rather than a comment:
#   (i)   DIRECTION. Two of the three alerts are LOW-is-bad (`plan_is_free == 0`,
#         `spend_probe_ok == 0`), so they bridge with `min_over_time`. The mechanical `max` port
#         reads the healthiest sample in the window and delays a real plan upgrade by the whole
#         range — CloudflareZonePlanNotFreeMaxDirection, asserted 10 minutes late in test 2.
#   (ii)  THE absent() ARM. CloudflareSpendProbeBlind's second arm produces a LABEL-LESS alert
#         instance, so an unbridged roll does not merely gap the alert — it swaps `{zone=…}` for
#         `{}` and back, which is a window restart with no change in the underlying condition.
#         Bridging the arm (`absent(min_over_time(…[10m]))`) is what removes it; test 3 pins the
#         transition itself with a promql assertion, not just the resulting alert.
#   (iii) THE COST OF DROPPING IDENTITY is NOT the masking #313 accepted. Both aggregations here
#         were chosen alert-preserving (`max` on a HIGH-is-bad gauge, `min` on LOW-is-bad ones), so
#         a healthy replica cannot hide a stuck one — the stuck one wins and the belt fires. What
#         is actually lost is the pod NAME in the alert's labels, and what is gained is a zone-wide
#         page when only one replica is affected. Test 6 asserts exactly that, and is the test to
#         change first if either Deployment is ever scaled out.
#
# ⚠ CloudflareSpendProbeBlind is FIRING IN PRODUCTION for a real cause while this lands (#231 —
# argo/smart_routing 401s, code 1015, both product zones blind). That is a different problem and
# #334 does not touch it: the same two zones fire before and after, verified against the live
# series on 2026-08-12. What does change for #231 is the alert's LABEL SET (no more pod/instance),
# so ArgoCD's sync resolves the two firing instances and re-fires them once under the new identity.
#
# NOT covered here (honest remaining work, in #334's PR body, swept by #351): CloudflareExporterDown
# — deliberately left in its per-target form, `up == 0` needs a live target and a replaced target is
# a genuinely new attempt at being scraped. The other alert this paragraph used to name,
# CloudflareEdge5xx, is GONE as of #350: it was never in this class either, but the reason it has no
# behaviour test is that `cloudflare_zone_requests_status` cannot be produced for any zone this
# account holds, so a fixture would only have asserted an expr against an invented series. The
# evidence and the re-add condition live in prometheusrule.yaml's header where the alert was.
rule_files:
  - spend-belt.promtool-rules

evaluation_interval: 1m

tests:
  # ── 1/7 — ONE spend-probe roll, all three alerts, both zones ─────────────────────────────────
  # The roll shape #288 measured (70-120s of vector-empty; a 2m hole here, with an explicit `stale`
  # marker — that is what kube SD writes when the old target disappears, and a plain end-of-series
  # would let PromQL's 5m lookback flatter the pre-fix form). Every gauge the pod exports gaps at
  # the same instant, because it is one pod: that is the whole reason this class exists.
  # One drift per zone, mirroring spend-probe.py's `_FLIPPED` fixture, so the test also proves
  # `by (zone)` selects the RIGHT zone instead of collapsing the two into one alert.
  - interval: 1m
    name: "a spend-probe roll no longer re-clocks the two toggle alerts' `for: 5m`"
    input_series:
      # Argo Smart Routing: ON for teststuff.net (the drift), off for minutark.ee (the decoy)
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_argo_smart_routing{zone="teststuff.net",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.166:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-7946494648-mp24c",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "1+0x2 stale"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_argo_smart_routing{zone="teststuff.net",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.171:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "_x5 1+0x120"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_argo_smart_routing{zone="minutark.ee",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.166:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-7946494648-mp24c",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "0+0x2 stale"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_argo_smart_routing{zone="minutark.ee",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.171:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "_x5 0+0x120"
      # plan: minutark.ee has been moved off free (the drift), teststuff.net is free (the decoy)
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_plan_is_free{zone="minutark.ee",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.166:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-7946494648-mp24c",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "0+0x2 stale"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_plan_is_free{zone="minutark.ee",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.171:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "_x5 0+0x120"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_plan_is_free{zone="teststuff.net",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.166:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-7946494648-mp24c",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "1+0x2 stale"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_plan_is_free{zone="teststuff.net",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.171:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "_x5 1+0x120"
      # …and the probe itself is healthy on both zones throughout: the roll is the only event
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok{zone="teststuff.net",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.166:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-7946494648-mp24c",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "1+0x2 stale"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok{zone="teststuff.net",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.171:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "_x5 1+0x120"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok{zone="minutark.ee",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.166:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-7946494648-mp24c",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "1+0x2 stale"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok{zone="minutark.ee",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.171:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "_x5 1+0x120"
    promql_expr_test:
      # mid-hole (t=4m), the identity swap the bridge removes: the bare arm says "the probe is
      # gone" and would start a label-less alert instance…
      - expr: absent(cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok)
        eval_time: 4m
        exp_samples:
          - labels: "{}"
            value: 1
      # …while the bridged arm still sees the outgoing pod's samples and stays quiet
      - expr: absent(min_over_time(cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok[10m]))
        eval_time: 4m
        exp_samples: []
    alert_rule_test:
      # `for: 5m` is honoured — the bridge does not make either toggle fire early
      - eval_time: 4m
        alertname: CloudflareZoneSpendToggleEnabled
        exp_alerts: []
      - eval_time: 4m
        alertname: CloudflareZonePlanNotFree
        exp_alerts: []
      # on time at 5m, straight through the hole, and on the drifted zone only
      - eval_time: 6m
        alertname: CloudflareZoneSpendToggleEnabled
        exp_alerts:
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              platform_machinery: "true"
              zone: teststuff.net
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Usage-billed toggle enabled on Cloudflare zone teststuff.net"
              description: "Argo Smart Routing is no longer \"off\" on zone teststuff.net — a per-GB usage-billed feature, which bills the card attached to the account. SYMPTOM ONLY. Check: Cloudflare audit log for who/when (docs/cloudflare.md §Token matrix lists which tokens carry Zone Settings Write), then GET /zones/{id}/argo/smart_routing to confirm the live value."
      - eval_time: 6m
        alertname: CloudflareZonePlanNotFree
        exp_alerts:
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              platform_machinery: "true"
              zone: minutark.ee
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Cloudflare product zone minutark.ee is no longer on the free plan"
              description: "Zone minutark.ee reports a plan other than free — a recurring charge on the card attached to the account. SYMPTOM ONLY (a deliberate upgrade looks identical to an accidental one). Check: Cloudflare audit log, and whether the change was intended; the two watched zones are the product zones only, eid-demo.com is out of scope by design."
      # one continuous instance each, not two
      - eval_time: 20m
        alertname: CloudflareZoneSpendToggleEnabled
        exp_alerts:
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              platform_machinery: "true"
              zone: teststuff.net
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Usage-billed toggle enabled on Cloudflare zone teststuff.net"
              description: "Argo Smart Routing is no longer \"off\" on zone teststuff.net — a per-GB usage-billed feature, which bills the card attached to the account. SYMPTOM ONLY. Check: Cloudflare audit log for who/when (docs/cloudflare.md §Token matrix lists which tokens carry Zone Settings Write), then GET /zones/{id}/argo/smart_routing to confirm the live value."
      # a healthy probe never trips the blind alert, and the bridged absent() arm does not invent
      # one out of the roll
      - eval_time: 6m
        alertname: CloudflareSpendProbeBlind
        exp_alerts: []
      - eval_time: 45m
        alertname: CloudflareSpendProbeBlind
        exp_alerts: []
      # THE WITNESSES: both pre-#334 forms are silent when the shipped alerts page…
      - eval_time: 6m
        alertname: CloudflareZoneSpendToggleEnabledPre334
        exp_alerts: []
      - eval_time: 6m
        alertname: CloudflareZonePlanNotFreePre334
        exp_alerts: []
      - eval_time: 9m
        alertname: CloudflareZoneSpendToggleEnabledPre334
        exp_alerts: []
      # …and page only 5m after the NEW pod's first sample (5m + 5m), under a per-pod identity that
      # no longer matches the one that was pending. 5 minutes lost to a 2-minute roll, on a window
      # that is only 5 minutes long.
      - eval_time: 11m
        alertname: CloudflareZoneSpendToggleEnabledPre334
        exp_alerts:
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              zone: teststuff.net
              container: probe
              endpoint: http-metrics
              instance: 10.244.2.171:9505
              job: cloudflare-spend-probe
              namespace: monitoring
              pod: cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n
              service: cloudflare-spend-probe
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Usage-billed toggle enabled on Cloudflare zone teststuff.net"
      - eval_time: 11m
        alertname: CloudflareZonePlanNotFreePre334
        exp_alerts:
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              zone: minutark.ee
              container: probe
              endpoint: http-metrics
              instance: 10.244.2.171:9505
              job: cloudflare-spend-probe
              namespace: monitoring
              pod: cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n
              service: cloudflare-spend-probe
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Cloudflare product zone minutark.ee is no longer on the free plan"

  # ── 2/7 — THE DIRECTION, the part of this port that is not mechanical ────────────────────────
  # `plan_is_free == 0` is LOW-is-bad, so the alert-preserving bridge is `min_over_time`: the
  # WORST sample in the window wins, and a plan upgrade is seen the moment it is scraped. The
  # mechanical `max_over_time` port keeps reporting the last healthy `1` for the whole range, so it
  # cannot even start its `for: 5m` until the range has rolled over — ten minutes of a recurring
  # charge nobody has been told about, on the one belt whose job is to notice a charge starting.
  # The pre-#334 form is checked here too, and it is the point of the pairing: on the ENTRY edge
  # the bridge costs nothing at all, so the delay below belongs entirely to the wrong direction.
  - interval: 1m
    name: "the bridge direction matters: `min_over_time` pages at 26m, the `max` port at 35m"
    input_series:
      # free until t=20m, then someone upgrades minutark.ee to Pro
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_plan_is_free{zone="minutark.ee",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.166:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-7946494648-mp24c",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "1+0x20 0+0x100"
    promql_expr_test:
      # shipped: the 0 at t=21m is in every window from t=21m on, so the condition is true at once
      - expr: min by (zone) (min_over_time(cloudflare_zone_plan_is_free[10m]))
        eval_time: 21m
        exp_samples:
          - labels: '{zone="minutark.ee"}'
            value: 0
      # the mechanical port: the last `1` (t=20m) is inside (19m, 29m]…
      - expr: max by (zone) (max_over_time(cloudflare_zone_plan_is_free[10m]))
        eval_time: 29m
        exp_samples:
          - labels: '{zone="minutark.ee"}'
            value: 1
      # …and out of (20m, 30m], which is the first moment it can even start its window
      - expr: max by (zone) (max_over_time(cloudflare_zone_plan_is_free[10m]))
        eval_time: 30m
        exp_samples:
          - labels: '{zone="minutark.ee"}'
            value: 0
    alert_rule_test:
      - eval_time: 25m
        alertname: CloudflareZonePlanNotFree
        exp_alerts: []
      - eval_time: 27m
        alertname: CloudflareZonePlanNotFree
        exp_alerts:
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              platform_machinery: "true"
              zone: minutark.ee
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Cloudflare product zone minutark.ee is no longer on the free plan"
              description: "Zone minutark.ee reports a plan other than free — a recurring charge on the card attached to the account. SYMPTOM ONLY (a deliberate upgrade looks identical to an accidental one). Check: Cloudflare audit log, and whether the change was intended; the two watched zones are the product zones only, eid-demo.com is out of scope by design."
      # the entry edge is free: the pre-#334 form pages at the same minute, so nothing below is the
      # bridge's fault — it is the direction's
      - eval_time: 27m
        alertname: CloudflareZonePlanNotFreePre334
        exp_alerts:
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              zone: minutark.ee
              container: probe
              endpoint: http-metrics
              instance: 10.244.2.166:9505
              job: cloudflare-spend-probe
              namespace: monitoring
              pod: cloudflare-spend-probe-7946494648-mp24c
              service: cloudflare-spend-probe
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Cloudflare product zone minutark.ee is no longer on the free plan"
      # the mechanical port: silent when the shipped alert pages, silent nine minutes later…
      - eval_time: 27m
        alertname: CloudflareZonePlanNotFreeMaxDirection
        exp_alerts: []
      - eval_time: 34m
        alertname: CloudflareZonePlanNotFreeMaxDirection
        exp_alerts: []
      # …and paging at 30m + `for: 5m` = 35m, two whole windows late
      - eval_time: 36m
        alertname: CloudflareZonePlanNotFreeMaxDirection
        exp_alerts:
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              zone: minutark.ee
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Cloudflare product zone minutark.ee is no longer on the free plan"

  # ── 3/7 — THE absent() ARM TRANSITION, in the live #231 shape ────────────────────────────────
  # Today's production state (2026-08-12): both product zones blind, `spend_probe_ok == 0` on each,
  # CloudflareSpendProbeBlind firing for a real cause (#231 — argo/smart_routing 401s, code 1015).
  # Now roll the probe pod underneath that. The pre-#334 expr does something worse than gap: the
  # `== 0` arm empties AND the `absent()` arm turns true, so the alert trades two `{zone=…}`
  # instances for one label-less `{}` instance and back again — an identity change with no change
  # in the condition, which is a `for: 30m` restart by another route. The promql pair above the
  # assertions is that transition, executed at the instant it happens.
  # This case is the acceptance criterion "survives the `or absent()` arm transition" (#334).
  - interval: 1m
    name: "a roll no longer flips CloudflareSpendProbeBlind between per-zone and absent() identity"
    input_series:
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok{zone="teststuff.net",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.166:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-7946494648-mp24c",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "0+0x20 stale"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok{zone="teststuff.net",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.171:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "_x24 0+0x120"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok{zone="minutark.ee",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.166:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-7946494648-mp24c",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "0+0x20 stale"
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok{zone="minutark.ee",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.171:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
        values: "_x24 0+0x120"
    promql_expr_test:
      # mid-hole (t=22m): the pre-#334 arm pair swaps identity — the zone arm has nothing…
      - expr: cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok == 0
        eval_time: 22m
        exp_samples: []
      # …and the absent arm supplies a label-less instance in its place
      - expr: absent(cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok)
        eval_time: 22m
        exp_samples:
          - labels: "{}"
            value: 1
      # the shipped pair: the zone arm never lets go, so the absent arm never gets a turn
      - expr: min by (zone) (min_over_time(cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok[10m]))
        eval_time: 22m
        exp_samples:
          - labels: '{zone="teststuff.net"}'
            value: 0
          - labels: '{zone="minutark.ee"}'
            value: 0
      - expr: absent(min_over_time(cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok[10m]))
        eval_time: 22m
        exp_samples: []
    alert_rule_test:
      # `for: 30m` honoured…
      - eval_time: 29m
        alertname: CloudflareSpendProbeBlind
        exp_alerts: []
      # …and paged on time at 30m, per zone, straight through the roll
      - eval_time: 31m
        alertname: CloudflareSpendProbeBlind
        exp_alerts:
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              platform_machinery: "true"
              zone: minutark.ee
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Cloudflare spend-toggle belt is blind on zone minutark.ee"
              description: "The spend-toggle probe has not read a zone's plan/Argo state for 30m — the gauges above are UNKNOWN, not safe, and a toggle flipped now would go unnoticed. SYMPTOM ONLY. Check: pod + logs (deploy/cloudflare-spend-probe in monitoring, it logs every failed read), the cloudflare-exporter-token Secret (ESO ← Infisical CLOUDFLARE_OBSERVABILITY_READ), then the token's Zone Settings Read on both product zones (docs/cloudflare.md §Token matrix)."
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              platform_machinery: "true"
              zone: teststuff.net
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Cloudflare spend-toggle belt is blind on zone teststuff.net"
              description: "The spend-toggle probe has not read a zone's plan/Argo state for 30m — the gauges above are UNKNOWN, not safe, and a toggle flipped now would go unnoticed. SYMPTOM ONLY. Check: pod + logs (deploy/cloudflare-spend-probe in monitoring, it logs every failed read), the cloudflare-exporter-token Secret (ESO ← Infisical CLOUDFLARE_OBSERVABILITY_READ), then the token's Zone Settings Read on both product zones (docs/cloudflare.md §Token matrix)."
      # THE WITNESS: silent at the same moment — its two zone windows died with the old pod and the
      # 3-minute `{}` instance the absent() arm raised in their place never reached `for: 30m`
      - eval_time: 31m
        alertname: CloudflareSpendProbeBlindPre334
        exp_alerts: []
      - eval_time: 53m
        alertname: CloudflareSpendProbeBlindPre334
        exp_alerts: []
      # …and it re-pages 30m after the new pod's first sample (24m + 30m), 24 minutes late, on a
      # condition (#231) that was continuously true the whole time
      - eval_time: 55m
        alertname: CloudflareSpendProbeBlindPre334
        exp_alerts:
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              zone: minutark.ee
              container: probe
              endpoint: http-metrics
              instance: 10.244.2.171:9505
              job: cloudflare-spend-probe
              namespace: monitoring
              pod: cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n
              service: cloudflare-spend-probe
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Cloudflare spend-toggle belt is blind on zone minutark.ee"
          - exp_labels:
              severity: warning
              zone: teststuff.net
              container: probe
              endpoint: http-metrics
              instance: 10.244.2.171:9505
              job: cloudflare-spend-probe
              namespace: monitoring
              pod: cloudflare-spend-probe-6b8d5c9f42-q7x2n
              service: cloudflare-spend-probe
            exp_annotations:
              summary: "Cloudflare spend-toggle belt is blind on zone teststuff.net"

  # ── 4/7 — the probe VANISHES (FU-150), and the price the bridged absent() arm charges ────────
  # The other half of the absent() arm's job, and the one place bridging it costs something: pod
  # deleted, ESO secret pulled, Deployment scaled to zero. Absence is still the alert — but the
  # bridge holds the last reading for the range first, so the label-less instance starts 10 minutes
  # later than it used to and the page lands at ~50m instead of ~41m.
  # ACCEPTED, and the asymmetry is the argument: a probe that is GONE is also visible as
  # CloudflareExporterDown and as a missing Deployment, while the roll this range exists for
  # happens on every ArgoCD sync of a `replicas: 1` workload. Ten minutes on the rare failure buys
  # a window that no longer restarts on the routine one.
  - interval: 1m
    name: "a probe that disappears still fires through absent(), 10m later than the unbridged arm"
    input_series:
      - series: 'cloudflare_zone_spend_probe_ok{zone="teststuff.net",container="probe",endpoint="http-metrics",instance="10.244.2.166:9505",job="cloudflare-spend-probe",namespace="monitoring",pod="cloudflare-spend-probe-7946494648-mp24c",service="cloudflare-spend-probe"}'
